Provides max HP based on current Endurance. The formula is as follows, for Endurance E:

The need for rounding is due to the HP provided varying by Endurance level:

From 2 to 15, ranks of Endurance usually grant 8 HP but sometimes grant 7 but both happen;

From 31 to 60, ranks grant 2 HP more often than they grant 1, but both happen;

From 61 to 100, ranks grant 1 HP slightly more often than they grant 0 but both happen (Endurance 100 grants 0, so the perk stops scaling at 99).

E1 gains the most HP (10, double that of going from E1 to E2); the first +7 happens at E5 (going from E3 to E4 grants more than going from E4 to E5, but E5 to E6 is another +8), the first +1 happens at E32, and the first +0 happens at E62. The graph shown to the left removes the rounding to show the shape of the curve.
